12. CPU  hub

What your processor is, how busy it is, and who keeps it busy.

On your machine
  CPU       11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1165G7 @ 2.80GHz · 8 logical CPUs
  Load      1.25, 0.90, 0.62 over 1, 5 and 15 minutes, for 8 CPUs
  Tasks     2 running right now, 1043 in all
  Governor  powersave

Commands
  nproc            number of CPUs you can use
  lscpu            model, cores, threads and caches
  uptime           load average over 1, 5 and 15 minutes
  top              busiest processes; press 1 for one line per CPU
  mpstat -P ALL 1  usage of each CPU every second (package sysstat)

Paths
  /proc/cpuinfo             one block per logical CPU
  /proc/loadavg             load average and task counts
  /sys/devices/system/cpu/  online CPUs, frequency, governor

Cards
  idk 12.1  Load average
  idk 1.2   How the kernel shares the CPUs
  idk 1.4   Interrupts: how devices get attention
  idk 10.3  nice and priorities
